text:
morgan: heads-up: customers hitting runtime error when using our JS SDK from Next.js middleware: "TypeError: crypto.subtle is not a function"

ivey: thanks, saw that in a support ticket. repro is Next 13 middleware deployed to Vercel Edge. Local node server ok.

morgan: repro steps I used: create middleware.ts, `import { createClient } from 'redwood-inference'`, deploy — request fails during import. stack points to signing helper that calls Node crypto APIs.

kevin: root cause: a helper still does `import { randomBytes } from 'crypto'` / uses Buffer in a few spots. Edge runtimes only expose WebCrypto and lack node builtins.

nina: quick mitigation for customers: lazy-check for Web Crypto and only import SDK after verifying it. Example for Next Edge middleware:

```js
// middleware.ts (Next Edge)
export async function middleware(req) {
  if (!globalThis.crypto || !globalThis.crypto.subtle) {
    // fail fast so user sees clear message
    return new Response('Edge runtime missing Web Crypto. See SDK docs.', { status: 500 });
  }
  const { handler } = await import('redwood-inference/edge'); // edge ESM entry
  return handler(req);
}
```

kevin: long-term: we should publish an ESM-only edge entrypoint that never references node built-ins. Proposal: add "./edge": "./dist/edge/index.mjs" to package.json exports, build with esbuild/tsup to replace Node helpers with WebCrypto implementations, and emit `dist/edge/index.d.ts`.

morgan: also consider adding a small runtime check in the edge entry that will throw a clear error if WebCrypto is absent so users don't hit opaque stack traces.

ivey: TS note: Next Edge customers often forget to include DOM lib so TS doesn't know about `crypto.subtle`. Recommend docs snippet:

```
// tsconfig.json
{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "lib": ["ES2021", "DOM"],
    "module": "esnext"
  }
}
```

kevin: build details: produce a separate rollup/tsup target that stubs imports of `crypto`, `fs`, `path` for the edge build (or outright removes code paths). Add a unit check to CI that scans `dist/edge` for any `require(` or `from 'crypto'` strings. If found, fail.

nina: docs + onboarding: add a short troubleshooting section in the Next sample app README and a one-liner in the main SDK README: "Edge runtimes (Next middleware) do not include Node built-ins — use the SDK edge export or lazy-load after verifying Web Crypto." This should reduce PV support noise.

morgan: one more gotcha: avoid top-level imports of the SDK in middleware files. Next will evaluate modules eagerly in some builds; lazy import pattern recommended.

sdk-bot: created issue #1421 "edge: publish WebCrypto-only ESM entry + Next middleware docs" — assigned to @kevin. :white_check_mark:

kevin: I'll open a PR with dist/edge build, types, exports map, and a tiny smoke test that runs a minimal Edge handler in CI (using `@vercel/edge-runtime` or `miniflare` in Node). If the smoke test is flaky, we'll at least include the static scan to prevent regressions.

nina: great — I'll update onboarding and the sample app to use the lazy import example and add the tsconfig hint.

morgan: thanks all — keeping this thread as the reference for the docs snippet and PR tracking.
